{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1520848-possibly-m5","id":1520848,"title":"\"Possibly\" M5","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-08-17T17:24:14-07:00","id":1520848,"title":"<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/icons/icon5.png\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" alt=\"\" /> \"Possibly\" M5","content":"This was something that crossed my mind and making it clear that I don't want to imply anything by this, I'm just talking about a thought of mine. Using the W5 as a base, what would the M5 look like if it had to also strip away its cultural traits? Traditions have a lot to do with belief so I really find it surreal to think about taking that away from them, I can imagine the Hermetics as a more traditional mage archetype, or SoE as technomages, the Verdana as a druid archetype, and maybe the euthanatos as vigilantes or necromancers, but while for the rest? Thinking now about technocracy I imagine them turning into a kind of illuminati that manipulates the world from the shadows for the personal gain of their leaders and who want to monopolize the use of magic and that's why they persecute the mages. Their SI would be an order of witch hunters or knights templars who wield magic, but it comes from the faith, or so they believe, basically the chorus. Anyway, this strange concept came to mind, how do you think it would be?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-17T22:31:34-07:00","id":1520854,"title":"","content":"It's probably gonna be awful just like V5, H5, and W5 were. Hell, it'll probably the worst one of the entire lot with the trajectory each gameline has taken,<br /> <br /> On a more specific note, I think they'll have it to be where the Nephandi can be redeemed but the Celestial Chorus will merge with the Knights Templar and get the &quot;Always Chaotic Evil&quot; treatment that the Fenrir got in W5. <br /> <br /> Dreamspeakers will be renamed and still declared unplayable anyway.<br /> <br /> I give a 50/50 shot on the Technocracy going one of two ways.<br /> <br /> A. They will be a ridiculous strawman caricature that's less of an actual faction and more of a walking political cartoon.<br /> <br /> B. They will get the &quot;secretly a good guy all along treatment&quot; or at least a &quot;still not as evil as those dang dirty Get of Fenris...I mean Celestial Choristers!&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm just a trans guy and gaming fan, unabashed hedonist and unusually upbeat nihilist, fairly laid back. He/Him.<br /> <br /> If everything is political, then nothing is!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25920-matt-corleone","name":"Matt Corleone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25920_8.webp","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-18T00:50:33-07:00","id":1520858,"title":"","content":"If they decouple Mage factions from their cultural roots, it will effectively cease to be Mage: The Ascension.<br /> <br /> Hypothetically, you could make a Werewolf: The Apocalypse game where Garou tribes aren't specific to any given culture or ethnic group, and still have it hit many of the same beats. (It would require you to keep around things like making deals with spirits and fighting the Wyrm/Pentex/Black Spiral Dancers. So, not W5 in the slightest).<br /> <br /> Everything about Mage: The Ascension revolves around the way it roots itself in Real Life cultural practices. The draw of playing MtAs, more than in other splats, is this authentic specificity. The degree to which it uses actual world views and practices to inform your characters.<br /> <br /> To flatten Mage groups, as they've done with Vampires, Hunters, and Werewolves would be abominable. It's a waste of the greatest asset MtAs has going for it. If I wanted to play as a non-specific Wizard or Druid, I'd play more D&amp;D.<br /> <br /> I guarantee M5 will go this direction, too. Not just because it's been the modus operendi of WoD5 so far, but because Paradox has exhibited profound cowardice when it comes to portraying non-European cultures. To make MtAs work requires a deft hand and lots of research and cultural consulting. Sounds like a lot of work. Not to mention asking experts for their input and following through with it.<br /> <br /> Paradox won't even keep a Werewolf tribe playable if it's patterned after a Native American culture, even when they've got folks telling them how to do it well. Do you think Paradox will have what it takes to do the Dreamspeakers justice? Would they even try? Or will we see more erasure of these cultures, in a misguided attempt to dodge controversy?<br /> <br /> Also, imagine the worst examples of Enforced Street Level Play from the Revised era, post Avatar Storm. M5 would almost certainly top that. Forget potentially getting your Avatar shredded by the Avatar Storm, you're unlikely to be allowed to attempt Stepping Sideways at all. Getting off the Streets and into anywhere else is BadWrongFun.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":10}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-18T02:31:27-07:00","id":1520864,"title":"","content":"At an educated guess from what we've seen so far<br /> <br /> -Stronger emphasis on street setting in both lore and mechanics.<br /> <br /> -the traditions are more a pc class than culture<br /> <br /> -the nine mt's discredited as a unified force in some context. most likely both morally and practically.<br /> <br /> -Paradox dice will sit on your pool like hunger dice<br /> <br /> -They'll be some sort of supplementary maintenance mechanic which will have negative ramifications if used,<br /> <br /> -touchstones.<br /> <br /> -Umbral jaunts strongly discouraged both in setting and mechanics<br /> <br /> -way less fun gonzo stuff<br /> <br /> -Union play will either be impossible or strongly discouraged. clumsy links with irl politics based on middle class nerd anxieties established.<br /> <br /> -magic system severly nerfed. even if you can still theorectically do <i>everything</i> it will be very hard to do <i>anything</i><br /> <br /> <br /> Less sure about but likely<br /> <br /> -Nephandi and mauraders will be more mysterious<br /> <br /> -stronger emphasis on orphans<br /> <br /> -some clumsy writting in relation to anti vax.<br /> <br /> -Vaguely written unhelpful lore<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-18T03:25:11-07:00","id":1520867,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Psicose</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1520848-possibly-m5#post1520848\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This was something that crossed my mind and making it clear that I don't want to imply anything by this, I'm just talking about a thought of mine. Using the W5 as a base, what would the M5 look like if it had to also strip away its cultural traits? Traditions have a lot to do with belief so I really find it surreal to think about taking that away from them, I can imagine the Hermetics as a more traditional mage archetype, or SoE as technomages, the Verdana as a druid archetype, and maybe the euthanatos as vigilantes or necromancers, but while for the rest? Thinking now about technocracy I imagine them turning into a kind of illuminati that manipulates the world from the shadows for the personal gain of their leaders and who want to monopolize the use of magic and that's why they persecute the mages. Their SI would be an order of witch hunters or knights templars who wield magic, but it comes from the faith, or so they believe, basically the chorus. Anyway, this strange concept came to mind, how do you think it would be?</div> </div> </div> </div>Attempting a somewhat more positive take on this: maybe Mage character creation will do away with explicit mention of the Traditions during character creation and will instead feature Approaches a la <b>Mage Made Easy</b>? Instead of choosing between Akashic Brotherhood, Celestial Chorus, Cult of Ecstasy, Dreamspeakers, Euthanatos, Order of Hermes, Sons of Ether, Verbena, or Virtual Adepts, the code you're offered goes more along the lines of Devotee, Ecstatic, Mad Scientist, Magus, Martial Artist, Necromancer, Reality Hacker, Shaman, or Witch. Or perhaps M20's Focus mechanics will be out front and center, with the point in the process where you'd expect to select your faction instead asking you to craft a Paradigm and a Practice? Again, no mention there is the Traditions by name; just a selection of Practices that roughly correspond to them: e.g., Faith, High Ritual Magick, Invigoration, Martial Arts, Reality Hacking, Shamanism, Weird Science, Witchcraft, and Yoga.<br /> <br /> With the Traditions listed as footnote examples: e.g., \u201cThe Celestial Chorus is a faction of Faithful mages/Devotees who prize ecumenism above all else, while the Templars are a fraction of Faithful mages/Devotees who derive from the legendary Knights of the Temple.\u201d","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 08-18-2023, 08:34 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-18T03:50:43-07:00","id":1520868,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bluecho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1520848-possibly-m5?p=1520858#post1520858\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If they decouple Mage factions from their cultural roots, it will effectively cease to be Mage: The Ascension.<br /> <br /> Hypothetically, you could make a Werewolf: The Apocalypse game where Garou tribes aren't specific to any given culture or ethnic group, and still have it hit many of the same beats. (It would require you to keep around things like making deals with spirits and fighting the Wyrm/Pentex/Black Spiral Dancers. So, not W5 in the slightest).<br /> <br /> Everything about Mage: The Ascension revolves around the way it roots itself in Real Life cultural practices. The draw of playing MtAs, more than in other splats, is this authentic specificity. The degree to which it uses actual world views and practices to inform your characters.<br /> <br /> To flatten Mage groups, as they've done with Vampires, Hunters, and Werewolves would be abominable. It's a waste of the greatest asset MtAs has going for it. If I wanted to play as a non-specific Wizard or Druid, I'd play more D&amp;D.<br /> <br /> I guarantee M5 will go this direction, too. Not just because it's been the modus operendi of WoD5 so far, but because Paradox has exhibited profound cowardice when it comes to portraying non-European cultures. To make MtAs work requires a deft hand and lots of research and cultural consulting. Sounds like a lot of work. Not to mention asking experts for their input and following through with it.<br /> <br /> Paradox won't even keep a Werewolf tribe playable if it's patterned after a Native American culture, even when they've got folks telling them how to do it well. Do you think Paradox will have what it takes to do the Dreamspeakers justice? Would they even try? Or will we see more erasure of these cultures, in a misguided attempt to dodge controversy?<br /> <br /> Also, imagine the worst examples of Enforced Street Level Play from the Revised era, post Avatar Storm. M5 would almost certainly top that. Forget potentially getting your Avatar shredded by the Avatar Storm, you're unlikely to be allowed to attempt Stepping Sideways at all. Getting off the Streets and into anywhere else is BadWrongFun.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree. Magical practices are deeply tied to cultural practices. I don't see any way where you can take that away and keep the essence of mage the ascension. What I suspect is that they're going to turn the traditions more into general philosophies detached from culture as much as possible. I don't think there's anything wrong with this approach per se, but if you do this then you're creating a new line that has nothing to do with ascension. We're probably going to end with traditions that serve only as pillars for the typical magical archetypes from pop culture and with a setting that would fit in practically any urban fantasy world. As for the technocracy, if they remove their new nuance and make them pure antagonists then I won't even bother giving the new edition a chance.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2964,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2964-firanai","user":"Firanai","date":". 12-26-2023, 02:37 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2964-firanai","name":"Firanai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2964_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-18T04:43:19-07:00","id":1520869,"title":"","content":"Earlier editions have already done the \u201cstrip the Traditions of their cultures\u201d thing already, with such moves as having the Euthanatoi include factions from India, Scandinavia, and Ireland, or how the Dreamspeakers are \u201ca bunch of magical traditions from all over the world united only by their belief in animism\u201d. The Celestial Chorus lumps in anything that could remotely be considered monotheistic; and so on.<br /> <br /> I do agree, though, that they're probably going to turn the Technocracy into cardboard villains.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 08-18-2023, 07:51 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-18T04:43:55-07:00","id":1520870,"title":"","content":"I may be wrong, but I feel that they will find someway to shoehorn in touchstones.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"https://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.nodiatis.com/pub/18.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27313-hello","name":"Hello","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27313_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-18T05:01:31-07:00","id":1520871,"title":"","content":"Won't surprise me. Touchstones help keep you in touch with Sleepers and are a way to help combat hubris. <br /> <br /> Oh, and it won't surprise me if they try to make Hubris a mechanical thing, possible even to the extent of having <i>that </i>be the M5 equivalent of Hunger Dice. Less about Paradox, more about Resonance and \u201cwhat goes around comes around\u201d.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-18T05:25:39-07:00","id":1520873,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1520848-possibly-m5?p=1520869#post1520869\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Earlier editions have already done the \u201cstrip the Traditions of their cultures\u201d thing already, with such moves as having the Euthanatoi include factions from India, Scandinavia, and Ireland, or how the Dreamspeakers are \u201ca bunch of magical traditions from all over the world united only by their belief in animism\u201d. The Celestial Chorus lumps in anything that could remotely be considered monotheistic; and so on.<br /> <br /> I do agree, though, that they're probably going to turn the Technocracy into cardboard villains.</div> </div> </div> </div>That was more fleshing out than stripping away, the groups kept their core identity points while expanding into new areas M5 will almost certainly downgrade the Traditions as generic fantasy archeotypes eg order of hermes will just be generic fantasy wizards.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-18T05:33:26-07:00","id":1520874,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hello</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1520848-possibly-m5?p=1520870#post1520870\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I may be wrong, but I feel that they will find someway to shoehorn in touchstones.</div> </div> </div> </div>If I guess it'll be about stopping quiets it's way easier to wedge touchstones into mage than werewolf or even vampire so I'm a 100% they'll be showing up.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-18T10:07:20-07:00","id":1520895,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Matt Corleone</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1520848-possibly-m5?p=1520854#post1520854\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's probably gonna be awful just like V5, H5, and W5 were. Hell, it'll probably the worst one of the entire lot with the trajectory each gameline has taken,<br /> <br /> Dreamspeakers will be renamed and still declared unplayable anyway.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think the traditions would drop to seven or six at that point, with the Dreamspeakers gone, with the Adepts and the SoE being one faction, the chorus being something else, and the Akashic brotherhood, I don't even know if you can do anything with them .<br /> <br /> In this case the spheres would look like:<br /> Order of Hermes - Forces<br /> Euthanatos - Entropy or Fate<br /> SoE - Time and Space (In case they would be a single sphere for both)<br /> Verbena - Life and Mind (In case the two would be the same sphere)<br /> Ecstasy? - Matter<br /> ??? - Spirit (Or they could put the hollow ones)\u200b<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-18T15:25:22-07:00","id":1520905,"title":"","content":"Also, not only will the Choristers get merged with the Knights Templar and given the uber-villain treatment that the Fenrir got in W5, but I also think the Hollow Ones and the Verbena will be championed and lionized to just as great of an extent. Especially the Hollow Ones.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm just a trans guy and gaming fan, unabashed hedonist and unusually upbeat nihilist, fairly laid back. He/Him.<br /> <br /> If everything is political, then nothing is!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25920-matt-corleone","name":"Matt Corleone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25920_8.webp","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-18T15:40:24-07:00","id":1520906,"title":"","content":"\u2026and I'll just note, before unsubscribing, that this has become (or always was?) A \u201cbitch and moan\u201d thread \u2014 supposedly targeted at an as yet unannounced product, but actually ragging on an existing, but different, gameline. <br /> <br /> Bye, folks! Have fun\u2026<br /> \u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},