ic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1520848-possibly-m5?p=1520906#post1520906\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u2026and I'll just note, before unsubscribing, that this has become (or always was?) A \u201cbitch and moan\u201d thread \u2014 supposedly targeted at an as yet unannounced product, but actually ragging on an existing, but different, gameline.<br /> <br /> Bye, folks! Have fun\u2026<br /> \u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>I kind of just had that thought and tried to guess... and that's it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-18T17:21:21-07:00","id":1520913,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1520848-possibly-m5?p=1520909#post1520909\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Once bitten twice shy as they say...</div> </div> </div> </div>Is that a proverb?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-18T17:25:20-07:00","id":1520914,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Matt Corleone</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1520848-possibly-m5?p=1520905#post1520905\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, not only will the Choristers get merged with the Knights Templar and given the uber-villain treatment that the Fenrir got in W5, but I also think the Hollow Ones and the Verbena will be championed and lionized to just as great of an extent. Especially the Hollow Ones.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that just if they were changed enough, the Hollow Ones would have to become sort of revolutionary or cynics or both. The Verbena I think only if they become that vegan stereotype, which already deviates from their original proposal, at least according to what I saw in Rev.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-19T05:34:10-07:00","id":1520938,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Psicose</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1520848-possibly-m5?p=1520913#post1520913\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Is that a proverb?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah it means repeated negative experiances will make you wary of simular events","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","user":"Ragged Robin","date":". 08-19-2023, 08:53 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-19T08:17:21-07:00","id":1520946,"title":"","content":"Certain fashions box people in creatively. Just look at the grimdark and &quot;realistic&quot; trends in superhero comics in the 1990s. At first they were novel. Now they're total bores. So, you've made superman evil and killed him, for the forty third time, (yawn) this week.<br /> <br /> The changes most of us fear for a possible M5 would be dull cliches. Street Level mages in a grimdark future of despair. It's old and tired and passing off as daring and original is a bore.<br /> <br /> Something more like the Second Edition is more what the customers want.<br /> <br /> I'd love to see the <b>Tales of Dark Magick</b> series tried again. Offer instructions on how to fit the game to your preferred narratives.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":857,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","user":"Astromancer","date":". 08-19-2023, 11:24 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-19T09:11:56-07:00","id":1520950,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1520848-possibly-m5?p=1520869#post1520869\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Earlier editions have already done the \u201cstrip the Traditions of their cultures\u201d thing already, with such moves as having the Euthanatoi include factions from India, Scandinavia, and Ireland, or how the Dreamspeakers are \u201ca bunch of magical traditions from all over the world united only by their belief in animism\u201d. The Celestial Chorus lumps in anything that could remotely be considered monotheistic; and so on.</div> </div> </div> </div>Earlier editions didn't strip away their cultures, they <i>added</i> to them. They made the Traditions <i>more</i> nuanced, by giving <i>more</i> touchpoints with Real Life cultural practices.<br /> <br /> What Paradox has been doing, and what it will likely do with M5, is take away connections to Real Life. <i>Flatten</i> the setting and its participants, not deepen them. That is the difference.<br /> <br /> Anyone could play a &quot;broad strokes&quot; version of a fantasy mage archetype. It was perfectly acceptable. It's just that if you wanted to dig deeper, you could go <i>very deep</i>. Because Real Life magical practices are stranger and more nuanced than anything a game developer could make up. As MtAs went on, it added more reference points for the Tradition archetypes at play. So it was easier to play a Mage in a deep way, if you wanted to.<br /> <br /> M5 is set to make playing a broad and nonspecific mage character non-optional. You WILL play a generic, street level urban fantasy character with a magic system cribbed from a used book store's New Age aisle. Or M5 has nothing to offer you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-19T10:58:59-07:00","id":1520962,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1520848-possibly-m5?p=1520908#post1520908\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't think the chorus will go villain, the union already fulfil the extremist mage antagonist role the get and Sabbat cover in their equivelant. I actually think it's unlikely they'll do much dramatic with the Celestial except maybe downplaying links with christianity specifically.<br /> they might merge vebrenna and dreamspeakers however into an outsider folk wizard tradition.</div> </div> </div> </div>See, I disagree with the Union being the extremist Mage villain role for M5 since the Sabbat was already a very antagonistic force in the original Vampire but they still got the Fenrir treatment.<br /> <br /> The Get of Fenris got turned into the biggest villains ever in W5, moreso than even the BSD's or Pentex, and they even made the Swords of Heimdall camp into the entirety of the Fenrir. <br /> <br /> The &quot;Cult of Fenris&quot; bullshit is what makes me think the Technocratic Union will be a shallow one-note attack on capitalism like Pentex was in W5 but the Celestial Chorus will get the &quot;irredeemable Always Chaotic Evil fascists&quot; treatment instead.<br /> <br /> If they're including the Disparate Alliance garbage from M20, I expect the Sisters of Hippolyta to get merged with the Verbena and will be treated as &quot;Always Lawful Good&quot; along with the Hollow Ones (since Hollow Ones always were the &quot;street level&quot; angsty goths and punks even back in Mage 2e)<br /> <br /> Parawolf/Renegade has shown their true colors on this one.<br /> <br /> If Karim Muammar was willing to turn the entirety of the Get of Fenris into the Swords of Heimdall (who were seen as a despised fringe even within 1e and 2e) to promote his own personal beliefs and agendas, then I honestly think he will do the same with the Celestial Chorus.<br /> <br /> Not only do I think M5 will not de-emphasize Christian influences in the Celestial Chorus, I think it will also over-emphasize the Christian aspects of the Choristers and will specifically make them out to be hardliner traditionalist Calvinist Protestants yet despite this will also somehow try to merge the very Catholic Knights Templar in with the Choristers because The Crusades were bad, m'kay?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm just a trans guy and gaming fan, unabashed hedonist and unusually upbeat nihilist, fairly laid back. He/Him.<br /> <br /> If everything is political, then nothing is!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25920-matt-corleone","name":"Matt Corleone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25920_8.webp","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-20T03:20:15-07:00","id":1521021,"title":"","content":"If M5 was modeled in the same way as H5 and W5 and following Justin Achilli's interpretation of MtAs (the core conflict is self-determination (Traditions) vs. authoritarianism (Technocracy) ), this is how I would picture M5:<ul><li>The Technocracy is winning</li> <li>The Technocracy is evil and is willing to accept all sorts of ills of humanity (misinformation, conspiracy theories, financial corruption, addiction to technology, environmental exploitation etc.) for the sake of maintaining control</li> <li>The Traditions have failed, especially the older, experienced Mages who are too stuck in their ways</li> <li>The only way to exist is to forge your own path to Ascension (the emphasis is on <i>individual </i>interpretations of Tradition-creeds rather than belonging to an organization)</li> <li>Ascension for humanity has never been further away</li> <li>Instead, helping and pushing individual people towards Ascension is the focus (aka &quot;street-level&quot;)</li> <li>Sphere-magic is severely limited by a PC's own perspective on their magic (the definition of what counts as &quot;vulgar&quot; is broadened)</li> <li>Paradox-dice are there to punish players for either trying to do magic outside their limited &quot;lane&quot; (defined by the PC's own perspective on their magic) or trying magic that's considered too powerful by the system</li> </ul>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-20T08:31:26-07:00","id":1521032,"title":"","content":"That sounds a lot like the premise behind MRev.<br /> <br /> I would like to think that M5 would take at least a few things from M20, such as the new Focus and Reality Zone systems. I <i>don't </i>see \u201cParadox Dice\u201d being used to punish a mage from straying from his <i>own</i> Focus \u2014 although that would be an interesting alternative to M20's Working Without Focus rule.<br /> <br /> If they <i>really</i> want to go with self-determination vs. authoritarianism, they ought to downplay the Traditions: go with Brucato's notion of playing independent mages as the default, with the Traditions and Crafts being entirely optional: put the choice of Focus in there instead of choosing which Tradition you belong to; and mention the Traditions, if at all, as footnotes to the the various Practices you can choose from: e.g., \u201ctwo significant factions of mages that practice High Ritual Magick are the Order of Hermes and the Wu Lung\u201d. You don't get more individualistic than that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 10-22-2023, 12:27 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-20T09:34:42-07:00","id":1521036,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1520848-possibly-m5?p=1521021#post1521021\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If M5 was modeled in the same way as H5 and W5 and following Justin Achilli's interpretation of MtAs (the core conflict is self-determination (Traditions) vs. authoritarianism (Technocracy) ), this is how I would picture M5:<ul><li>The Technocracy is winning</li> <li>The Technocracy is evil and is willing to accept all sorts of ills of humanity (misinformation, conspiracy theories, financial corruption, addiction to technology, environmental exploitation etc.) for the sake of maintaining control</li> <li>The Traditions have failed, especially the older, experienced Mages who are too stuck in their ways</li> <li>The only way to exist is to forge your own path to Ascension (the emphasis is on <i>individual </i>interpretations of Tradition-creeds rather than belonging to an organization)</li> <li>Ascension for humanity has never been further away</li> <li>Instead, helping and pushing individual people towards Ascension is the focus (aka &quot;street-level&quot;)</li> <li>Sphere-magic is severely limited by a PC's own perspective on their magic (the definition of what counts as &quot;vulgar&quot; is broadened)</li> <li>Paradox-dice are there to punish players for either trying to do magic outside their limited &quot;lane&quot; (defined by the PC's own perspective on their magic) or trying magic that's considered too powerful by the system</li> </ul></div> </div> </div> </div>I wouldn't use those words for traditions and technocracy, because it makes their relationship very black and white and I particularly think it's better when neither side is completely good, but I think that's what's in fashion.<br /> I don't know if giving freedom to each PC has for their vision of magic, because if we take an example like Harry Potter, all you need is a wand and know the name of the spell, in the Mage system that would be fine OP, because hypothetically you can do anything without much difficulty, even worse if in the person's conception he can do anything just because yes, and seriously this is the conception of some, so I think that the rules established by the traditions for focus should just remain with a personalization depending on the person.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-20T09:36:53-07:00","id":1521037,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Psicose</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1520848-possibly-m5?p=1521036#post1521036\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I wouldn't use those words for traditions and technocracy, because it makes their relationship very black and white and I particularly think it's better when neither side is completely good, but I think that's what's in fashion.<br /> I don't know if giving freedom to each PC has for their vision of magic, because if we take an example like Harry Potter, all you need is a wand and know the name of the spell, in the Mage system that would be fine OP, because hypothetically you can do anything without much difficulty, even worse if in the person's conception he can do anything just because yes, and seriously this is the conception of some, so I think that the rules established by the traditions for focus should just remain with a personalization depending on the person.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is addressed in M20 by the Focus system; you don't need Traditions for this.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-20T10:19:13-07:00","id":1521039,"title":"","content":"I've actually been giving this a lot of thought recently. I agree that it would be all be impossible to divorce the Traditions from their cultural roots. They are just too ingrained for some of them, although I do think that the Dreamspeakers could be saved, as their Tradition was not founded in a specific geographical location as many of the other ones. I've been experimenting with tying a Mage's Avatar in a way that V5 does with Predator Type, i.e. having a Avatar drive a Mage into getting certain traits even before Awakening and giving bonus die to those traits based a irl magical archetypes. For instance, a Pattern Avatar Mage following the Alchemist archetype would get an extra dot in Matter, an extra dot in either Stamina or Manipulation, an extra dot in Science or Persuasion, and an extra dot in Resources. This alchemist Mage would also get bonuses in casting Matter effects and gain dots in Matter faster than other spheres.<br /> This of course would mean that one doesn't get their Primary sphere from their Tradition. Instead, they would get possible Secondary Spheres that they would learn a little slower than their primary, but still faster than other spheres. Instead, a Mage would get an Initiation similar to a Legacy Attainment from M:tAw, a magical effect that would not trigger Paradox. Each such Initiation would give a Major function that would cease to function if they changed Traditions, and a Minor function that could possibly stay with them otherwise. This Initiation would also have some sort of drawback that could cause problems in the long run either to the Mage themselves or how they interact with others. Such abilities have been hinted at, such as how Dreamspeakers can interact with Changelings and the Dreaming without being enchanted, but have never been fully explored.<br /> These changes are just the basic ones I've thought about that wouldn't break the game too badly, but I'm still afraid that M5 could be the one that really could end the new editions for a lot of people, although I have spotted some fans elsewhere on social media that 'like' how the new games are doing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>THWarted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/17984-toby-weingarten","name":"Toby Weingarten","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-20T10:45:02-07:00","id":1521042,"title":"","content":"M20 has already divorced Primary Sphere from Tradition; so to me, that's a non-issue: Traditions haven't been the determinators of a mage's Magick for about ten years now. <br /> <br /> I <i>do</i> think that there ought to be more to Avatars and their relationship to the mage; but I'd leave it up in the air as to whether the Avatar guided the mage toward a particular Focus before the Awakening, or if the proto-mage's experiences and Awakening shaped the nature of the Avatar. Either way, the Avatar ought (normally) to be compatible with the mage's Focus; if it isn't, you have something akin to M20's Demented Eidolon Flaw, but more generalized. One thing I could see them doing would be to say that Avatars can be altered, kind of like how Mage: the Awakening allows mages to shape their souls to get Attainments. But in Mage: the Ascension, this generally isn't a <i>good</i> thing: it's a generalization of the Inverted Avatars of the Nephandi and the Permanent Quiet of the Marauders. I would, in this way, say that a Technocrat's Genius is a similarly altered Avatar, but with the effect being less blatant: it \u201cmerely\u201d results in the Genius being Circumspect and the Technocrat not manifesting Supernatural Merits. <br /> <br /> Have you seen the STV supplement <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/446015\" target=\"_blank\">Prism of Focus</a>? In it, each Practice is assigned a strength and a weakness \u2014 one thing that it's especially good at, and another thing that it's not so good at. It also has Specialized Practices, variants of the standard Practices developed by various Traditions, Conventions, and Crafts that gain an additional benefit above and beyond what the standard Practice normally provides. I'd like to see something along these lines implemented in M5. <br /> <br /> But the more I think about it, the less need I see for the Traditions themselves: nearly everything that I found useful about them in the earlier editions it's handled by Focus in M20; and going back to the M1e/2e/Rev centrality of Tradition to Magick would be a massive step backward, IMHO.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-20T11:09:01-07:00","id":1521046,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1520848-possibly-m5?p=1521037#post1521037\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This is addressed in M20 by the Focus system; you don't need Traditions for this.</div> </div> </div> </div>I learned it at e3 so I'll owe you that one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-20T13:02:08-07:00","id":1521056,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1520848-possibly-m5?p=1520906#post1520906\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u2026and I'll just note, before unsubscribing, that this has become (or always was?) A \u201cbitch and moan\u201d thread \u2014 supposedly targeted at an as yet unannounced product, but actually ragging on an existing, but different, gameline.<br /> <br /> Bye, folks! Have fun\u2026<br /> \u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, can you really be upqet ar MtA fans of all people to see a pattern?<br /> <br /> V5 shattered the community<br /> H5 is a product unworthy of a proffessional studio<br /> W5 is bad beyond words<br /> <br /> And all the things that are bad about them, and appearing everywhere in the 5th editions, all have the smell of &quot;we'll specifically wreck Mage&quot;.<br /> <br /> Unless parawolf get their collective head out of the paradox realm that their collective ass have become, predicting the worse for future 5th ed gamelines is the best way of thinking","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24043-nyremne","name":"Nyremne","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"414"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-20T13:16:55-07:00","id":1521058,"title":"","content":"I <i>am</i> a Mage fan. And I also have no love for V5 or H5. (I can't comment on W5 because I haven't seen it for myself yet; but what I've heard about it isn't encouraging.) So I absolutely get \u201cseeing a pattern\u201d and \u201conce bitten, twice shy\u201d.<br /> <br /> But the comments I was seeing earlier in this thread were excessive even for that. It felt like there was a competition to see who could voice the most offensive take on what <s>W5 was like</s> M5 would be like.<br /> <br /> Incidentally: the reason I'm still around is two-fold: first, when I went to unsubscribe from the thread, I found that I wasn't subscribed to it: I'm subscribed to the <i>forum, </i>meaning that I'm being bombarded by the sheer negativity of the worst of this thread whether I like it or not; and second, there have been some subsequent posts that aren't so abrasive about crapping all over the games. I'm willing to engage with those; but I have no intention to engage with anyone from the <i>gleefully</i> \u201cdown with ParaWolf!\u201d camp.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 08-20-2023, 04:32 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-20T13:34:51-07:00","id":1521061,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1520848-possibly-m5?p=1521058#post1521058\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But the comments I was seeing earlier in this thread were excessive even for that. It felt like there was a competition to see who could voice the most offensive take on what <s>W5 was like</s> M5 would be like.</div> </div> </div> </div>Is it really excessive when W5 went beyond our worst fears? <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24043-nyremne","name":"Nyremne","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"414"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-20T13:45:22-07:00","id":1521062,"title":"","content":"Yes. <br /> <br /> Compare the tone of this thread with the tone of the W5 thread that's going on on the Werewolf forum right now. Both are complaining about what was done to Werewolf. But the one on the Werewolf thread is doing so with thoughtful criticisms about W5; this thread is doing so through snark. And again, it's doing so on the Mage forum, under the guise of criticizing a game that, as far as I know, hasn't even been <i>announced </i>yet. Which is why I say that the weirdly specific snark isn't really targeted at Mage at all, but it's really just using Mage as a stand-in for their dissatisfaction with W5. <br /> <br /> So it's not just annoying; it's <i>off-topic</i> and annoying.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-20T14:19:44-07:00","id":1521065,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1520848-possibly-m5?p=1521062#post1521062\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes.<br /> <br /> Compare the tone of this thread with the tone of the W5 thread that's going on on the Werewolf forum right now. Both are complaining about what was done to Werewolf. But the one on the Werewolf thread is doing so with thoughtful criticisms about W5; this thread is doing so through snark. And again, it's doing so on the Mage forum, under the guise of criticizing a game that, as far as I know, hasn't even been <i>announced </i>yet. Which is why I say that the weirdly specific snark isn't really targeted at Mage at all, but it's really just using Mage as a stand-in for their dissatisfaction with W5.</div> </div> </div> </div>The snark is entirely deserved. Each and every 5th ed game showed how willing the authors were to butcher the original game to fit a badly imagined version.<br /> <br /> It's also not about W5, you may feel that because of the timing, but most (I would say 90%) of the snark here about M5 already existed after the release of V5. It came back when H5 showed it's ugly face, and now with W5.<br /> <br /> But it's not about either of those. It's simply us seeing the pattern and anticipating the inevitable rampage that will be M5.<br /> <br /> The snark isn't directed toward W5, it's directed toward Parawolf.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1520848-possibly-m5?p=1521062#post1521062\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So it's not just annoying; it's <i>off-topic</i> and annoying.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's on topic, since it's about the inevitable downfall of MtA when it's 5th edition will come to wear it's butchered skin.<br /> <br /> As for annoying, I'm sorry that it annoys you, but it's clearly cathartic for a lot of us. After all, there's little we can do about the incomming carnage of one of our beloved game except bet on the specific of the murder.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24043-nyremne","name":"Nyremne","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"414"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-20T14:22:18-07:00","id":1521066,"title":"","content":"Again, I'm also a Mage fan; stop speaking to me as if I don't know what's likely to be coming.<br /> <br /> \u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200bBut whether or not you think the snark is deserved, it's <i>still</i> excessive.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 08-20-2023, 05:43 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/42