Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-23T12:56:39-07:00","id":1521273,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1520848-possibly-m5?p=1521242#post1521242\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Don't confuse snark with criticism. You can do the latter without the former. I know you can, because you're doing so in the W5 thread.</div> </div> </div> </div>And why should we do criticism without snark? Because *you* dislike snark?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1520848-possibly-m5?p=1521242#post1521242\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This thread has been hijacked by posters who aren't just criticizing ParaWolf; they're using over the top claims \u2014 again, about a game that hasn't even been announced yet.</div> </div> </div> </div>You're being dishonest here. You know there's a pattern of terrible V5 games. There's no need to wait for the announcement of M5 to make evidence based preditions.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1520848-possibly-m5?p=1521242#post1521242\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And then they're shouting down anyone who asks them to tone it down a bit. Nobody's telling you to shut up or to refrain from criticizing; only to be a bit more civil about it.<br /> <br /> In fact, the only one who has been told to shut up is me.</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay, you really need to take a rest, now you're straight out lying.<br /> <br /> No one is shooting you down, no one asked you to shut up. You voiced criticism of the snark, and people answered back. You complained about tyhe snark, and I stated the fact that you're not forced to read it (ironically, the same way you said we were not forced to react the way we do) Nothing more.<br /> <br /> And again, you don't ask people to be civil. Being snarky isn't being uncivil.<br /> <br /> You're inventing a drama that doesn't exist. The fact is, we're rightfully anticipating the disaster that is M5, with all the snark deserve for the massacre of a beloved IP, and you don't like it. That's all. <br /> And again, no one forces you to be here, in fact, you said earlier you wanted out of the conversation. And yet you're still here.<br /> <br /> So if that conversation is that painful to you, you're free to not come on this thread. And if you stay on this thread, don't pretend you're asking us to be civil.<br /> <br /> We are civil, you just don't like what we're saying.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24043-nyremne","name":"Nyremne","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"414"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-29T20:19:31-07:00","id":1521641,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1520848-possibly-m5?p=1520869#post1520869\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Earlier editions have already done the \u201cstrip the Traditions of their cultures\u201d thing already</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I could see that - focusing on the Tradition's beliefs rather than the culture that may have spawned those beliefs. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I do agree, though, that they're probably going to turn the Technocracy into cardboard villains. </div> </div> </div>I am more convinced that the Technocracy moves into the shadows and becomes more of a boogie-man and manipulator than HITMarks in the streets. I think that Mages are going street-level and that the Union's crazy science stuff is going to be downplayed. Maybe Blackhats show up occasionally, but mostly Mages have to deal with an enemy entrenched in the world - finding their labs and strongholds is much harder.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9255-docsteve2020","name":"DocSteve2020","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"25"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-10T07:36:50-07:00","id":1522344,"title":"","content":"<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Psicose</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1520848-possibly-m5#post1520848\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">... what would the M5 look like if it had to also strip away its cultural traits? Traditions have a lot to do with belief so I really find it surreal to think about taking that away from them, I can imagine the Hermetics as a more traditional mage archetype, or SoE as technomages, the Verdana as a druid archetype, and maybe the euthanatos as vigilantes or necromancers, but while for the rest? Thinking now about technocracy I imagine them turning into a kind of illuminati that manipulates the world from the shadows for the personal gain of their leaders and who want to monopolize the use of magic and that's why they persecute the mages. Their SI would be an order of witch hunters or knights templars who wield magic, but it comes from the faith, or so they believe, basically the chorus. Anyway, this strange concept came to mind, how do you think it would be?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm going all the way back to the OP on this one because I think it's an interesting question <i>without</i> the (I think <i>mostly</i> deserved) negativity that comes from association with the other [x]5 lines.<br /> <br /> I think it's interesting because we've seen a Mage game where the magic, and the groups practicing it, were separated from real-world beliefs and practices, and it was called Mage: the Awakening. How did that game accomplish it? By creating a shared culture/history/conflict for all Mages, and splitting the Traditions into<ul><li>Orders, which are about goals, politics, attitude toward Sleepers, and <i>philosophy of power</i></li> <li>Paths, which are about where your power comes from and what that says about your strengths and weaknesses as an individual Mage.</li> </ul>(until Magical Traditions came along and explicitly introduced real-world magical practices again, but stick with me)<br /> <br /> Awakening Mages are participants in and products of real-life cultures, but <i>magic</i> is the legacy of an older, original culture. So where the Order of Hermes originated in the court wizards (/Thoth-priests) of pharonic Egypt, the predessors of the Mysterium <i>supplied</i> those court wizards. Critically, it's <i>objectively true (</i>if sometimes metaphorical). And THAT is the most critical break from Ascension, where magic being <i>subjective</i> is the whole darn point of the game line. Ascension magic is comes from real-life cultural associations because <i>Mages</i> come from those cultures, so their <i>beliefs</i> come from those cultures, so their <i>magic</i> comes from those cultures.<br /> <br /> So, there's an easy path for M5 to trim out cultural associations - become more like Awakening. Make &quot;Mages&quot; a culture of their own and magic a secret-but-objectively-real force/spirit/concept that culture knows about and can harness. In an Ascension context this would imply more mechanics-awareness and genre-savviness than Ascension Mages are supposed to have... because it implies that I know my paradigm is just window dressing over a deeper truth, which means I don't really <i>believe</i> in it<i>, </i>which means it <i>shouldn't work</i>. This is an age-old problem in Mage, and big swaths of Storytellers' Guides have been spent addressing it.<br /> <br /> So is there another way to keep magic subjective while removing the cultural links from which magical philosophies come, so we don't lose so much of the unique character of Mage? Maybe. Possibly you could focus less on the <i>Orders-like </i>side of Traditions and more on the <i>Path-</i>like side of Paradigm - how do <i>I </i>harness my magic? First place my brain goes here is Foundations from DA:M. So imagine the usual Spheres, but a Foundation-like stat with the high-concept focus of an Awakening Path in place of Arete. <i>Just </i>enough mechanical enforcement to create a cross-cultural common ground for magic without completely steamrolling different practices. So in this world, the Order of Hermes is a western cultural order (kind of like a Legacy) grown up around a shared Obrimos-like Foundation - with sympathies toward other groups with related cultural heritage <i>or</i> who share their Foundation. Groups like the Spirit-Talkers, Ecstatics, and Euthanatos are already cross-cultural and fit into this architecture well - they're bound together by a shared Path/Foundation (attitudes that are vaguely Thrysus-like, Mastigos-like, and Moros-like, respectively) but their local expressions are very different.<br /> <br /> Hermetics, Verbena, and Akashics probably need the most finessing, but that's because they <i>started</i> as so culturally-specific. I think resolving this is about opening the door <i>wider - </i>what would <i>other</i> cultural expressions of the fundamental Path/Foundation of those groups look like? I think there is a fair case that Hermetics and Choristers are different faces of the &quot;Obrimos-like&quot; command-and-power coin, for example. The two groups have deep historical connections anyway, and you could easily split them along philosophies of <i>command</i>: Choristers <i>invoke</i> power while Hermetics <i>evoke</i> power. Probably lots of good drama there between the two groups. It may be too reductive, but I could see a read on the Akashics that also made them into a very <i>different</i> expression of command/power Obrimos approach (Awakening certainly thinks so) - replacing the hammer with a scalpel, command as in &quot;command of ones faculties&quot; rather than &quot;I command you&quot;.<br /> <br /> If we bring inspiration from DA:M's Spontaneity, Verbena fit into a spot like Awakening's Acanthus - choice, consequence, agency. Are they the only such? Maybe the VAs represent moving the Connection seat on the Council to the choice/consequence VAs from the Mastigos-heavy Al-i-Batin?<br /> <br /> (NOTE! I'm not advocating for any of these particular changes or approaches in M5. I'm just musing on how I would approach a writing challenge like <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar27832_1.jpg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"27832\" data-vbnamecard=\"27832\">Psicose</a> presents)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":456,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/456-blackwell","user":"Blackwell","date":". 09-10-2023, 04:38 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/456-blackwell","name":"Blackwell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar456_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"977"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-10T10:27:37-07:00","id":1522346,"title":"","content":"It looks functional. At least at first glance.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],